WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.760
 Yeah, I mean, I think we all have a lot

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:04.080
 of good ideas in the medical

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.600
 establishment of how to

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.370
 control blood pressure, how to convince

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:09.680
 people to care about blood pressure, but

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:10.640
 it's a lot more

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.380
 about understanding where community

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.170
 members are and meeting them where they

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:15.440
 are. So I think a huge

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.260
 crux of the problem we're trying to solve

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:21.230
 for is more community engagement, more

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:22.240
 listening sessions,

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.900
 embedding ourselves deeper before we

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.710
 introduce the medical piece. And a lot of

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:28.080
 our newest

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.540
 iteration or newest model is going to be

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.850
 based on like really a deep sustained

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.000
 effort to build

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.650
 relationships before we even introduce

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:39.520
 medications. But it's a complex problem

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.040
 to try to get people

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.960
 that have issues with food insecurity and

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:47.200
 violence in the home to care about an asymptomatic

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:47.440
 risk

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.420
 factor like hypertension. So a lot of it

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:51.360
 is like understanding where they are,

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:52.000
 what's important to

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.440
 them, addressing their social barriers,

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:56.430
 and then introducing treatment for

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:57.440
 hypertension,

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:00.120
 you know, when we have their trust.

